{
  "configuration_id": "config_027",
  "reason": "Evidence: Our best result so far is config_028 (scvi_n200, resnet50, concat, singleprofile) at 0.5362 acc. We know RNA dominates (0.4849 rna_only vs 0.2079 image_only), and the multimodal gain over RNA-only is modest (~4 pts for pca_n2000). We have only tested concat fusion across all multimodal runs, so the effect of fusion strategy is completely uncharacterized. Question: config_027 (scvi_n200, resnet50, weighted, singleprofile) changes only the fusion from concat to weighted relative to config_028, cleanly isolating the fusion effect. Why this is the best next experiment: Fusion is a fundamental design axis that will influence every future multimodal configuration. If weighted fusion outperforms concat, it suggests the weak image signal (0.2079 alone) benefits from learned down-weighting, and we should adopt weighted fusion going forward. If concat matches or exceeds weighted, we confirm simple concatenation is sufficient and can redirect budget toward testing the image encoder (ViT-L) or multiprofile aggregation. This single-variable comparison maximizes information gain per experiment under the limited budget."
}

